    "debrief.stages.2.title": "Count HTTP bytes using consistent filters",
    "debrief.stages.2.detail": "Four matching POSTs occur from 11:20:05 to 11:23:05, each with bytes_out=262144, totaling 1048576 bytes. Match source, host, method, and path; exclude GET /health, internal metrics, and response bytes_in.",
    "debrief.stages.3.title": "State the limits of correlation",
    "debrief.stages.3.detail": "Consistent sources, destination names, and times link activity across channels. It remains unknown whether mail size and HTTP uploads represent the same content, include sensitive data, or form legitimate synchronization.",
    "debrief.cause": "These records cannot distinguish endpoint compromise, credential misuse, and authorized business traffic. An unfamiliar external destination and service-account authentication are leads to investigate, not proof of a vulnerability or cause of data loss.",
    "debrief.impact": "The dataset records 1 MiB of HTTP uploads from the target client and acceptance of an 846120-byte mail message by an external destination. It does not establish the amount of unique leaked data or whether the recipient read it.",
    "debrief.limits.0": "A DNS query is not a successful connection or transmission.",
